' Pattern component notes
note top of DataAutonomyExample
  <b>Data Autonomy Pattern</b>
  - Owns its data storage (dealStore, userStore)
  - Controls data access through well-defined interfaces
  - Encapsulates internal data structures
  - Responsible for data validation and integrity
end note

note top of FunctionalAutonomyExample
  <b>Functional Autonomy Pattern</b>
  - Provides complete business capability (commission calculation)
  - Operates independently without external dependencies
  - Encapsulates all logic needed for its business function
  - Has well-defined interfaces for interaction
end note

